# Anything the Pi executes or parses must arrive with LF endings,
# whatever the machine that edited it. A shell script checked out with
# CRLF fails as `bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M`, and a systemd unit picks
# up a trailing \r on every value - ExecStart included. Both present as
# a file that looks perfect when you cat it.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.service   text eol=lf
*.rules     text eol=lf
